{"data":{"id":"10.5281/zenodo.20567719","type":"dois","attributes":{"doi":"10.5281/zenodo.20567719","prefix":"10.5281","suffix":"zenodo.20567719","identifiers":[],"alternateIdentifiers":[],"creators":[{"name":"Dietz, Joel","nameType":"Personal","givenName":"Joel","familyName":"Dietz","nameIdentifiers":[{"nameIdentifier":"0009-0007-4948-9192","nameIdentifierScheme":"ORCID"}],"affiliation":[]}],"titles":[{"title":"BioEval — Bioinformatics Paper Evaluator"}],"publisher":"Zenodo","container":{},"publicationYear":2026,"subjects":[{"subject":"reproducibility"},{"subject":"bioinformatics"},{"subject":"computational biology"},{"subject":"research software evaluation"},{"subject":"data transparency"},{"subject":"information theory"},{"subject":"swarm intelligence"},{"subject":"stigmergy"},{"subject":"agent-based simulation"},{"subject":"FAIR data"},{"subject":"large language models"}],"contributors":[],"dates":[{"date":"2026-06-08","dateType":"Issued"}],"language":"en","types":{"ris":"COMP","bibtex":"misc","citeproc":"article","schemaOrg":"SoftwareSourceCode","resourceType":"","resourceTypeGeneral":"Software"},"relatedIdentifiers":[{"relationType":"IsSupplementTo","relatedIdentifier":"https://github.com/fractastical/bioinformatics-eval","relatedIdentifierType":"URL"},{"relationType":"HasVersion","relatedIdentifier":"10.5281/zenodo.20567720","relatedIdentifierType":"DOI"},{"relationType":"HasVersion","relatedIdentifier":"10.5281/zenodo.20597158","relatedIdentifierType":"DOI"}],"relatedItems":[],"sizes":[],"formats":[],"version":"0.9.1","rightsList":[{"rights":"MIT License","rightsUri":"https://opensource.org/licenses/MIT","schemeUri":"https://spdx.org/licenses/","rightsIdentifier":"mit","rightsIdentifierScheme":"SPDX"}],"descriptions":[{"description":"This deposition is a version of the BioEval Reproducibility Report — an arXiv-style preprint that explains how the BioEval evaluation system works and presents its evaluations of a corpus of computational-simulation papers — bundled together with the complete, MIT-licensed source code of the system. Two files are included: the report PDF and a full archive of the source at the corresponding revision.\n\nComputational and agent-based simulation papers increasingly drive claims about biological coordination (ant and termite stigmergy, honeybee colony dynamics, firefly synchronization, ant-colony optimization), yet their reproducibility is rarely assessed systematically. BioEval is an LLM-driven framework that submits a paper by URL or PDF, extracts its real text (and errors out rather than scoring unextractable input), gathers external evidence, and scores the paper on a versioned seven-dimension rubric using Anthropic Claude.\n\nThe central question BioEval asks is whether a simulation accords with good data and reproducibility practice. Six dimensions measure exactly this: Data Disclosure (15%), Dataset Resolvability (12%), Code Availability \u0026 Versioning (12%), Code-to-Data Traceability (15%), Simulation Derivation Clarity (14%), and Reproducibility Package Quality (7%). Scores are anchored to verified external signals — accessions and DOIs resolved against Crossref and DataCite, live repository facts such as a detected license — rather than the paper's own claims, and the framework does not credit unverifiable assertions or invent unsubstantiated gaps.\n\nA seventh, orthogonal dimension, Information-Theoretic Rigor (25%), scores whether a paper formalizes and quantifies the information content of the system it models — Shannon entropy, mutual and transfer entropy, channel capacity, communication bit rate — which is particularly apt for swarm, stigmergy, and synchronization systems where information flow IS the phenomenon. It measures scientific-content rigor, not transparency; topics with no information-theoretic dimension are scored at a neutral baseline (~50 on the 0–100 scale) so non-applicability neither rewards nor punishes. In rubric v0.9.0 it carries the single largest weight of the seven dimensions, an intentional elevation that reflects that for this corpus the quantification of information flow is central to the science rather than a peripheral concern. The overall score is the weighted mean of the seven dimensions.\n\nThe bundled report applies the rubric (version 0.9.0) to fourteen insect-swarm and agent-based simulation projects, reporting the raw seven-dimension scores including per-paper information-theoretic rigor. Its headline finding is that transparency is uneven and reproducibility packaging consistently weak, while information-theoretic rigor is systematically low even across projects whose entire subject is communication and coordination.\n\nThis is report edition 0.9.1, a pre-1.0 release. The evaluation rubric remains at version 0.9.0 and the corpus scores are unchanged from the 0.9.0 report; edition 0.9.1 adds an appendix (Appendix B) recording the evaluated projects' authors' responses to per-paper GitHub-issue outreach. Rubric 0.9.0 revised the dimension weights of the earlier 0.8.0 release, elevating Information-Theoretic Rigor from 10% to 25%. Built as a pnpm monorepo: React + Vite frontend, Express 5 API, PostgreSQL + Drizzle ORM, contract-first OpenAPI/Orval codegen.","descriptionType":"Abstract"}],"geoLocations":[],"fundingReferences":[],"xml":"","url":"https://zenodo.org/doi/10.5281/zenodo.20567719","contentUrl":null,"metadataVersion":2,"schemaVersion":"http://datacite.org/schema/kernel-4","source":"api","isActive":true,"state":"findable","reason":null,"viewCount":0,"viewsOverTime":[],"downloadCount":0,"downloadsOverTime":[],"referenceCount":0,"citationCount":0,"citationsOverTime":[{"year":"2026","total":1}],"partCount":0,"partOfCount":0,"versionCount":3,"versionOfCount":1,"created":"2026-06-06T07:10:23.000Z","registered":"2026-06-06T07:10:24.000Z","published":"2026","updated":"2026-08-22T13:22:30.000Z"},"relationships":{"client":{"data":{"id":"cern.zenodo","type":"clients"}},"provider":{"data":{"id":"cern","type":"providers"}},"media":{"data":{"id":"10.5281/zenodo.20567719","type":"media"}},"references":{"data":[]},"citations":{"data":[]},"parts":{"data":[]},"partOf":{"data":[]},"versions":{"data":[{"id":"10.5281/zenodo.20567720","type":"dois"},{"id":"10.5281/zenodo.20597158","type":"dois"},{"id":"10.5281/zenodo.20567719","type":"dois"}]},"versionOf":{"data":[{"id":"10.5281/zenodo.20567719","type":"dois"}]}}}}